course: dictionary
lesson: 2214
title: Couplets: two lines that belong together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A couplet is a pair of lines of poetry that go together. Usually the two lines rhyme and have the same rhythm, so they sound neat when you read them aloud. Two lines make one small unit of a poem.
explain: Look at the context to spot a couplet. «Chūnlián are red New Year couplets, poems on red paper put up by the door before New Year.» The word couplets tells you these are poems, and the sentence says they are written on red paper and hung by the door. You can guess that a couplet is a short piece of verse.
explain: Poems often end with a closing couplet, which gives a strong, neat point. An old story says «nián» was a monster scared away by red and loud bangs, so people hang red couplets by the door. Poets use couplets to finish a thought, and the rhyme helps the reader feel that it is done.
fact: A couplet is a pair of lines of poetry that go together.
fact: A rhyming couplet has two lines that rhyme at the end and usually have the same rhythm.
fact: A closing couplet is the last two lines of a poem, and it often gives a strong, neat point.
fact: «Heroic couplet» means a pair of rhyming lines of ten syllables each.
fact: «Chūnlián» are red New Year couplets, poems on red paper put up by the door before New Year. In rare use, a couplet can also mean a pair of anything.
exercise: What is a couplet? | A kind of red paper | A whole book of poems | A single word in a line | *A pair of lines of poetry that go together
exercise: «Chūnlián» are red New Year couplets. Where are they put up? | In a school bag | Under the bed | *By the door before New Year | On a train
exercise: What is special about a rhyming couplet? | Its lines are written in a foreign language only | *Its two lines rhyme at the end | Its lines are both longer than a page | Its lines have no rhythm at all
test: Where does a closing couplet usually appear in a poem? | *At the end, giving a strong, neat point | At the start, before any other lines | In the title only | In the middle, to fill up space
test: How many syllables does each line of a heroic couplet have? | Five | *Ten | Twelve | Six
exam: Which meaning of couplet is the rare one? | A line of exactly ten syllables | *A pair of anything, such as a couplet of socks | A red poem hung by the door | A pair of lines of poetry that rhyme
